meta {
  name: Get Product by ID
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/6a38f614c3d65a5f868b1a06
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Accept: application/json
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.data.id: eq 6a38f614c3d65a5f868b1a06
  res.body.data.sku: eq BAG-10157
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-07 against "David's Dev Account". Run with
  `--env "Dev"`, after `Get Access Token (Dev)`.
  
  ## What it does
  `GET /api/v3/products/{identifier}` by the product's Mongo ObjectId
  (`6a38f614c3d65a5f868b1a06`, SKU `BAG-10157` — a pre-existing read-only
  fixture, not created by this test). Returns the full `ProductOutputDto`
  shape, including nested `attributes`, expanded `categories` are NOT
  included by default here (only `attributes`, `product_relationships`,
  etc. -- see the sibling "Get Product Subpath" requests for expanded
  category/asset data).
  
  ## Spec discrepancy found
  The live response's relationship field is named `product_relationships`,
  not `relationships` as `openapi_pimv3.json`'s `ProductOutputDto` declares.
  See `Search Products - Filters.bru` and
  `config/api-testing.config.md` quirk #13.
}
